.TH GITUP 1 "2026" "Gitup" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gitup \- graphical Git client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gitup
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ PATH ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Gitup
is a graphical Git client: a commit graph with real lane assignment, diffs with
syntax highlighting and word-level intra-line comparison, blame, file history
and search, staging by file, hunk or individual line, branches, tags, stashes,
merge, cherry-pick, revert, reset, a three-way conflict editor, interactive
rebase, submodules, and several repositories open at once in tabs.
.PP
Local work is done through libgit2. Anything that touches the network runs the
real
.BR git (1)
binary, so existing credential helpers, the SSH agent and the system keychain
apply without configuration. Without
.BR git (1)
on
.BR PATH ,
fetch, pull, push and clone report that it is unavailable; everything local
continues to work.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I PATH
Repository to open. With no argument, the working directory is used when it is
inside one \(em which is a convenience of launching from a terminal, and
correctly finds nothing when launched from a desktop.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GITUP_LOG
Log filter, for example
.BR gitup=debug .
Defaults to
.BR warn,gitup=info .
.TP
.B GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL
Honoured as
.BR git (1)
honours it, so the identity Gitup reads and writes is the one git uses.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/gitup/settings.toml
Preferences, the recent-repository list, and key bindings.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1)
.SH BUGS
Report at https://github.com/koneb71/gitup/issues
